{
  "title": "Parameter runes",
  "pages": [
    {
      "components": [
        {
          "type": "modopedia:header",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "text": "Parameter runes",
          "centered": true,
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "type": "modopedia:text",
          "x": 2,
          "y": 16,
          "width": 96,
          "line_height": 9,
          "text": "Parameter runes do not always produce an effect on their own. An OpDefinition may match them directly, or they may simply become a center's ParameterRune list."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "modopedia:text",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 96,
      "line_height": 9,
      "text": "• arrow: a common direction input; MomentumOp uses it for projectile direction and size.\n• arrow_up: SplitEmitOp can use the array face normal as an upward emission direction."
    },
    {
      "type": "modopedia:text",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 96,
      "line_height": 9,
      "text": "• engaging: the ElementOp entry point, accepting elemental runes such as mana, fire, water, earth, and wind."
    },
    {
      "type": "modopedia:text",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 96,
      "line_height": 9,
      "text": "• split: divides an emission path; drain, eliminate, fix, and revert participate in data semantics."
    },
    {
      "type": "modopedia:text",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 96,
      "line_height": 9,
      "text": "• cross, curl, and loop are general shape or persistence inputs whose effect depends on the matcher."
    },
    {
      "components": [
        {
          "type": "modopedia:image",
          "x": 20,
          "y": 8,
          "width": 60,
